No need to apply formally.  We're an open-source project with everything
available on github, including a backlog of issues that you're welcome
to start working on. :)

You might want to start reading up a bit on the project infrastructure
here:  https://github.com/kernelci/kernelci-doc/wiki

And for ideas of where to contribute with code/features/fixes, you could
start with the issue tracker at the main "kernelci-core" project:
https://github.com/kernelci/kernelci-core

Thanks for your interest, and look forward to working with you.

